{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "kind": "definition",
      "text": "ℋlres is a d‑by‑d real matrix representing residual streams.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000048"
      ],
      "defines": [
        "ℋlres"
      ],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "definition",
      "text": "ℋlpre is a 1‑by‑d real matrix that aggregates streams into the branch input.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000048"
      ],
      "defines": [
        "ℋlpre"
      ],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "definition",
      "text": "ℋlpost is a 1‑by‑d real matrix that distributes branch output back to streams.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000048"
      ],
      "defines": [
        "ℋlpost"
      ],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "definition",
      "text": "x0 denotes d repetitions of the initial input.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000048"
      ],
      "defines": [
        "x0"
      ],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "claim",
      "text": "When ℋlres, ℋlpre, ℋlpost all equal the matrix [1], the model reduces to a single‑stream residual connection.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000048"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [
        "ℋlres",
        "ℋlpre",
        "ℋlpost"
      ],
      "mentions": [],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "definition",
      "text": "The network learns parameters (αls, Wls, bls) for each stream type s∈{pre,post,res} to allow dynamic topology.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000049"
      ],
      "defines": [
        "αls",
        "Wls",
        "bls"
      ],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "definition",
      "text": "𝒫 is the Sinkhorn‑Knopp projection operator applied via 20 iterations.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000051"
      ],
      "defines": [
        "𝒫"
      ],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "definition",
      "text": "A matrix B in 𝖡d is orthostochastic when there exists an orthogonal Q such that each entry B_ij equals Q_ij squared.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000054"
      ],
      "defines": [
        "orthostochastic matrix"
      ],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "claim",
      "text": "For dimension n≥3, orthostochastic matrices form a proper non‑convex subset of 𝖡d.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000054"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [
        "orthostochastic matrix"
      ],
      "mentions": [],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "definition",
      "text": "Q, an orthogonal matrix of size ds, can be seen as a d×d block matrix where each block Q_ij is s×s.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000055"
      ],
      "defines": [
        "block matrix Q"
      ],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "definition",
      "text": "Φ_{d,s}(Q)_{ij} equals the average squared Frobenius norm of block Q_ij, i.e., (1/s) Σ_{k,l}(Q_ij)_{kl}^2.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000056"
      ],
      "defines": [
        "Φ_{d,s}(Q)_{ij}"
      ],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "equation",
      "text": "ℋlres = ℋlpre = ℋlpost = [1]",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000048"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "equation",
      "text": "B_ij = Q_ij^2",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000054"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "equation",
      "text": "ℋlpre = sigmoid(αlpre·𝐱l′·𝐖lpre + 𝐛lpre)",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000050"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "equation",
      "text": "ℋlpost = 2·sigmoid(αlpost·𝐱l′·𝐖lpost + 𝐛lpost)",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000050"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "equation",
      "text": "ℋlres = 𝒫( mat( αlres·𝐱̂l′·𝐖lres + 𝐛lres ) )",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000050"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "definition",
      "text": "𝒫go maps learned parameters (αlres,Wlres,blres) to a d×d mixing matrix using generalized orthostochastic matrices.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000052"
      ],
      "defines": [
        "𝒫go"
      ],
      "requires": [],
